{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-28-Jun-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "If 855 ÷ 15 − k + 32 × 5 = 1152 ÷ 16 × 111 ÷ 37, then the value of k is:", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "In an election between A and B, every fifth vote polled was marked as invalid by the machine. In the remaining votes, A wins the election with a margin of 2500 votes or 10% of the total votes polled, over B. If 90% of the invalid votes would have been in favour of B, then which of the following would have been the result of the election?", "options": [{"text": "A would have won by 3%", "added": false}, {"text": "A would have won by 8%", "added": false}, {"text": "B would have won by 8%", "added": false}, {"text": "B would have won by 3%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Find the simplified value of 5055 − (1002 ÷ 20.04).", "options": [{"text": "50.05", "added": false}, {"text": "4050", "added": false}, {"text": "5050", "added": false}, {"text": "5005", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The population of a city increases every year at the rate of 5%. If the population of the city is 16000, what will be the population after 2 years?", "options": [{"text": "17700", "added": false}, {"text": "17600", "added": false}, {"text": "17000", "added": false}, {"text": "17640", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "population-and-depreciation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the number of students in various courses in various cities A, B, C, D and E in India during the academic year 2022-2023. In city A, the number of students in Medicine is nearly what percentage of MBA?", "options": [{"text": "87%", "added": false}, {"text": "85%", "added": false}, {"text": "92%", "added": false}, {"text": "89%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A dishonest dealer professes to sell his goods at cost price but uses a false weight of 950 grams instead of 1 kilogram. His gain percentage is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "dishonest-dealer", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Find the value of 15% of 1.5 + 0.15 ÷ 0.1 + 0.01 of 1.1 × 0.5 + 2.5 × 25.", "options": [{"text": "6.42305", "added": false}, {"text": "62.2305", "added": false}, {"text": "77.2305", "added": false}, {"text": "64.2305", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 125%, then by what percentage will its surface area increase (correct to two decimal places)?", "options": [{"text": "509.54%", "added": false}, {"text": "409.76%", "added": false}, {"text": "406.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "506.25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Simplify", "options": [{"text": "46.29", "added": false}, {"text": "80.41", "added": false}, {"text": "70.25", "added": false}, {"text": "53.25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "If the three sides of a triangle are 12, 22 and m units, then which of the following is correct?", "options": [{"text": "10 ≤ m < 34", "added": false}, {"text": "10 ≤ m ≤ 34", "added": false}, {"text": "10 < m < 34", "added": false}, {"text": "10 < m ≤ 34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2508 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "2260 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "2550 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1580 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "80.84%", "added": false}, {"text": "80.95%", "added": false}, {"text": "91.95%", "added": false}, {"text": "90.86%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1998", "added": false}, {"text": "1898", "added": false}, {"text": "1658", "added": false}, {"text": "1785", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "A shopkeeper gives a discount of 12% on the purchase of 10 kg of sugar. The cost price of the sugar is ₹30/kg, and the marked price is ₹38/kg. The weighing machine of the shopkeeper is faulty, and it shows weight of 1 kg when the actual weight is 900 grams. Find the percentage profit of the shop keeper (rounded off to two decimal places).", "options": [{"text": "23.85%", "added": false}, {"text": "22.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "12.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "30.18%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "The distance (d) a moving body travels, varies directly with the time (t) when it moves. A train travels 72 km in 2 hours. Find the equation that relates d and t.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "A hollow sphere of external and internal diameters of 10 cm and 6 cm, respectively, is melted and made into another solid in the shape of a right circular cone of base diameter 10 cm. Find the height of the cone.", "options": [{"text": "13.68 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "16.68 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "14.68 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "15.68 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "140°", "added": false}, {"text": "135°", "added": false}, {"text": "150°", "added": false}, {"text": "125°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "±3", "added": false}, {"text": "±2", "added": false}, {"text": "±4", "added": false}, {"text": "±6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "The below table shows the number of trees of 3 different fruits, planted during 2018- 2022. Study the table carefully and answer the question based on it. What was the percentage increase in the number of mango trees planted in 2020 compared to the number of mango trees planted in 2018?", "options": [{"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "17.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "23.08%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "Simplify (4 + 4) × (4 ÷ 4) × (4 × 4).", "options": [{"text": "124", "added": false}, {"text": "130", "added": false}, {"text": "144", "added": false}, {"text": "128", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "The sum of two numbers is 28 and the sum of their squares is 528. Find the square root of the product of both the numbers.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "A train covers a distance of 850 metres in 45 seconds. Travelling at the same speed, how many kilometres will the train cover in an hour?", "options": [{"text": "69", "added": false}, {"text": "67.2", "added": false}, {"text": "67.5", "added": false}, {"text": "68", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "Applied to a bill for ₹1000, what is the difference between a discount of 40% and two successive discounts of 36% and 4%?", "options": [{"text": "₹154", "added": false}, {"text": "₹144", "added": false}, {"text": "₹14.40", "added": false}, {"text": "₹15.40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "Ronak and Riya can do a work in 12 and 18 days, respectively. They worked together for six days and then Ronak left. Find the time taken by Riya to complete the work.", "options": [{"text": "3 days", "added": false}, {"text": "5 days", "added": false}, {"text": "6 days", "added": false}, {"text": "7 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "Simplify the following expression.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "A certain sum of money is given at a certain rate of simple interest for 4 years. Had it been given at 11% higher rate for the same time, it would have fetched ₹1320 more. Find the sum (in ₹).", "options": [{"text": "4580", "added": false}, {"text": "3000", "added": false}, {"text": "2500", "added": false}, {"text": "3240", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "A person covers 11 km with a speed of 7 km/h, 25 km with a speed of 10 km/h and 30 km with a speed of 20 km/h. What is the average speed of the person?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "If four distinct positive numbers, a, b, c and d, in the order given are in proportion, then which of the following options is NOT correct?", "options": [{"text": "b, a, d and c, in the order given are in proportion.", "added": false}, {"text": "c, d, b and a, in the order given are in proportion.", "added": false}, {"text": "a, c, b and d, in the order given are in proportion.", "added": false}, {"text": "d, c, b and a, in the order given are in proportion.", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "(1 - cos2A) sec2A is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "cosec2A", "added": false}, {"text": "tan2A", "added": false}, {"text": "cos2A cot2A", "added": false}, {"text": "cot2A", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "Shiya invests ₹1,53,000, which is 30% of her annual income, in mutual funds. What is her monthly income (in ₹)?", "options": [{"text": "45,800", "added": false}, {"text": "42,500", "added": false}, {"text": "55,600", "added": false}, {"text": "52,300", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "In a class, there are 60 students. The average weight of the entire class is 42 kg. If there are 36 boys in the class and the average weight of all the boys is 50 kg, then what is the average weight (in kg) of all the girls?", "options": [{"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "Simplify the given expression.", "options": [{"text": "99235", "added": false}, {"text": "99980", "added": false}, {"text": "99020", "added": false}, {"text": "99999", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "If x – y = 25 and xy = 444, compute the value of x3 – y3.", "options": [{"text": "28,495", "added": false}, {"text": "48,925", "added": false}, {"text": "42,985", "added": false}, {"text": "26,725", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "A cylinder has a radius of 7 cm and the area of its curved surface is 396 cm2. The volume of the cylinder is:", "options": [{"text": "1381 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1391 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1386 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1396 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "Two towns P and Q are 275 km apart. A motorcycle rider starts from P towards Q at 10:00 a.m. at the speed of 25 km/h. Another rider starts from Q towards P at 12 noon on the same day at the speed of 20 km/h. At what time will they cross each other?", "options": [{"text": "1:15 p.m.", "added": false}, {"text": "3:00 p.m.", "added": false}, {"text": "4:30 p.m.", "added": false}, {"text": "5:00 p.m.", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "7∶5", "added": false}, {"text": "5∶7", "added": false}, {"text": "9∶7", "added": false}, {"text": "7∶9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "What is the length (in cm) of chord PQ in a circle with a radius of 7 cm, where a diameter AB and non-diameter chord PQ intersect perpendicularly at point C, and the ratio of AC to BC is 4 : 3?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "A man travels 1200 km by train at 80 km/h, 1600 km by ship at 40 km/h, 1000 km by plane at 400 km/h, and 200 km by car at 50 km/h. What is the average speed for the entire distance? (rounded off to 2 decimal places)", "options": [{"text": "65.04 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "72.40 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "68.14 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "75.40 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "–1", "added": false}, {"text": "–2", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "82.39%", "added": false}, {"text": "76.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "74.19%", "added": false}, {"text": "78.20%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "Manish, Nakul and Pintoo alone can complete a certain work in 21days, 28 days and 15 days, respectively. Manish and Pintoo started the work together while Nakul joined them after 5 days and worked with them till the completion of the work. For how many days did Nakul work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "If tan θ + cot θ = 6, then the value of tan2θ + cot2θ is ____ .", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "If the sides of a triangle are 7, 12 and x, and x is an integer, then find the number of possible values of x.", "options": [{"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4.04% less", "added": false}, {"text": "4.04% more", "added": false}, {"text": "3.03% less", "added": false}, {"text": "3.03% more", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "On the tag price, a seller offers a 10% discount and a cashback of ₹250. He still earns 10% profit. If the cost price is ₹1,200, then the tag price (rounded off to 2 decimal places) is ₹______.", "options": [{"text": "1774.44", "added": false}, {"text": "1777.44", "added": false}, {"text": "1744.44", "added": false}, {"text": "1447.44", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}]}